---
description: Auto-ship every coherent unit of work
alwaysApply: true
---
- After you finish each coherent unit of work (a feature, fix, or docs change), commit locally with: `npm run ship -- "type(scope): summary"` using Conventional Commits (`feat` `fix` `docs` `style` `refactor` `perf` `test` `build` `ci` `chore` `security`), with a body explaining WHY.
- Default `npm run ship` is scan + commit locally. Do not push from ship.
- Run `npm run finish` **once** at the end of the task (pull --rebase, push, watch CI once). Not after every commit.
- Update README/docs in the same commit as any behavior change.
- Never use `--no-verify`. Never force-push. Never commit `.env*`, keys, tokens, or `*.pem`.
- If the secret scan blocks a commit, fix the cause. Do not bypass it. If a real key was ever exposed, tell the user to rotate it.
- Never read `.env*` files or print environment variables.
- Keep commits small: one idea each.
- If CI is red after `npm run finish`, fix it before doing anything else.
